Z||000001||2xsess||11-05-2000||06:52 PM||||I believe IMSA stands for International Motor Sports Assoc., I'm not sure though.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||11-05-2000||07:58 PM||||I don't know how accurate I have my facts, but supposedly in the mid 80's, Pontiac took a couple Fieros and designed a tubular racing chassis, plus lots of other racing mods and body mods in order to make competitive IMSA racing prototypes. Racers used these plans to build a small number of these unique Fiero race cars. Hopefully other guys will add more info or correct me if I'm wrong. Check out my web page for pics of a couple real IMSU cars.<P> <A HREF="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/imsa" TARGET=_blank>http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/imsa</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||11-05-2000||08:00 PM||||IMSA is a series of racing. Back in the late 80's Fiero's were used with SD4 racing engines in the GTU class. There are a few places selling the IMSA body kit for the Fiero. It has wider fenders, lower front airdam, and a wrap around spoiler. V-8 Archie had a white IMSA bodied car with a V-8 in it and FieroDave has an 85GT with the body kit on it. The REAL IMSA cars were tube frame strictly race cars. Bob Earl was one of the more popular racing Fiero drivers.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-05-2000).]||||reg||1
